ce1bf9706b6aa18435e2baccab63bdd72299257c (paths: src/quant_pipeline/...).

Operator directive (DECISIONS.md item 7): encode a full K8-uniform
routed-expert payload set with the SAME calibration / transform seed /
profile parameters as the K6 campaign, so future multi-precision K6K8 is
offline assembly from the two complete per-choice payload sets.  Uniform K8
keeps every single-rate invariant - this patch is ADMISSION ONLY:

  * glm53_direct_k4: SUPPORTED_BITS += 8; malaiwah-namespaced K8 recipe id,
    contract / materialization-plan / materialization-receipt / launch-plan
    schemas; the bits!=4 launch-plan branch of build_contract parameterized
    (bits==6 behavior byte-identical).
  * glm53_uniform_k8 (NEW module, entirely ours): K4-KL-gated K8/TP4 launch
    plan mirroring glm53_uniform_k6, with same_transform_seed_as_k6_campaign
    and the assembly-parts-bin purpose sealed into the plan.
  * glm53_mcg_preparation + glm53_prepared_backend: SUPPORTED_BITS += 8
    (GSS/encode paths are already bits-parameterized).
  * glm53_mtp_k4: malaiwah K8 MTP-contract / MTP-adapter / main-receipt
    schemas; launch-plan verify dispatch for bits==8.
  * glm53_packed_k4_reader: SUPPORTED_BITS += 8 - the trellis shape check
    [in/16, out/16, bits*16] and unpack_trellis_states are parametric, so
    bits=8 means 128 int16 words per tile with no further change; the K8 MTP
    adapter schema mirrors glm53_mtp_k4.
  * codecs/exl3_mcg: rate admission (3,4,5,6) -> (3,4,5,6,8).  The K8 pack
    of the accepted reconstruction closure was bit-verified against
    exllamav3 c5d9c657 native convert (fallback/VALIDATION.md V4/V9).
  * runtime/glm53_tp2_exl3 (serving-time admission, trivially safe): bits=8
    -> TP4, checkpoint bits tuple, trellis words (64,96) -> (64,96,128).
    The K8 serving path itself is qualified later (qualify_k8), like K6.
  * checkpoint/glm53_mcg_materializer needs NO hunks: plan/receipt schemas
    come from the patched glm53_direct_k4 helpers and every other bits use
    is parametric (the per-shard receipt schema f-string mints
    quant-pipeline.glm53-k8-materialized-shard-receipt.v1, minted and
    verified only inside that module - disclosed here).

Every K8 identifier that names a sealed artifact is malaiwah-namespaced;
none of upstream's sealed verifiers are weakened, and no K4/K6 code path
changes behavior.  Interior parametric f-strings shared with K4/K6 (work
units, offline-reader identity, shard receipts) stay parametric and are
disclosed in the campaign receipts.

IMPORTANT (reader-ABI binding): this patch modifies the reader FILE whose
byte hash the sealed K6 choices bind (decoder.reader_abi_sha256).  It must
land on a campaign tree only AFTER convert_k6 fully completes (or before a
campaign starts) - stage_k6.sh enforces this ordering.

